# .dev.vars.example — TEMPLATE for local Worker secrets/config. Placeholders only.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (that file is gitignored — NEVER commit it):
#        cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#   2. Fill in real values in `.dev.vars` for local `wrangler dev`.
#   3. For PRODUCTION, do NOT put secrets in wrangler.jsonc (it is committed).
#      Set each one with:
#        npx wrangler secret put NAME
#      Wrangler stores it encrypted; it becomes available on `env.NAME` at runtime.
#
# SECRET vs CONFIG
#   - Secrets (tokens, keys)      -> `.dev.vars` locally, `wrangler secret put` in prod.
#   - Non-secret config (origins) -> `[vars]` / "vars" in wrangler.jsonc is fine.
#
# CURRENT STATE
#   SimZoner has NO secrets today. It uses Cloudflare BINDINGS (AI, VECTORIZE, DB,
#   CONFIG), not API keys, so this file is a template only — nothing below is
#   required to run the Worker. The entries are illustrative EXAMPLES so the pattern
#   is documented for when a real secret is eventually needed.

# --- EXAMPLE ONLY (hypothetical; not used by the app today) ---------------------
# If we ever route Workers AI through an authenticated AI Gateway, its token would
# be a real secret and would live here / in `wrangler secret put`:
# AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN=replace-with-real-token

# --- EXAMPLE ONLY (non-secret config; could also live in wrangler.jsonc "vars") -
# Production frontend origin the CORS allowlist should permit (see src/security.ts).
# PROD_ORIGIN=https://simzoner.pages.dev
